Subject: [PATCH] feat(nemotron_h): per-run switches that swap one MoE piece for a reference version

The first on-chip check of Nemotron 3 Ultra on a v5p-64 read 2.62 to 12.08
times transformers' own BF16 error at slots 4 to 7. The pieces that run
differently on a TPU are the Pallas top-k kernel, the grouped matmul kernel,
and float32 dots left at the default precision. Each switch below swaps one
of them for a plain JAX version, so one engine start per setting names the
piece. The fault turned out to sit in the CPU reference, which rounded the
float32 router bias to BF16, and against the rebuilt reference all 108
layers passed on 2026-09-28 (models/nemotron3-ultra.md).

layers/moe_probe.py reads SGL_PROBE_TOPK, SGL_PROBE_GMM, SGL_PROBE_ROUTER,
SGL_PROBE_LATENT, SGL_PROBE_MOE, SGL_PROBE_SHARED, SGL_PROBE_MOE_OUT and
SGL_PROBE_MATMUL when the model traces. All are off by default, and a run with
none set traces the program the tree traced before. SGL_PROBE_TOPK=jnp turns the
Pallas top-k kernels off in layers/gate.py. SGL_PROBE_GMM=xla runs each routed
expert's matmuls as a masked dense dot per local expert, with float32
accumulation and gmm's output dtypes, and xla32 keeps the up projection and the
activation in float32 too. SGL_PROBE_ROUTER=f32highest computes the router's dot
as an explicit float32 dot_general at HIGHEST and writes the sigmoid out.
SGL_PROBE_LATENT=f32 runs fc1_latent_proj and fc2_latent_proj in float32 at
HIGHEST, so fc2's dot doesn't round the float32 expert output to BF16 on a TPU.

The v5p-64 run of those four on 2026-09-27 left slots 2 to 7 where the baseline
put them. SGL_PROBE_MOE=dense takes EPMoE's dispatch out: each shard runs every
local expert over every token in float32 at HIGHEST, scales each row by the
token's float32 top-k weight for that expert, and sums, with no sort by expert,
group sizes, padding, gmm or unpermute; the reduce over the tensor and expert
axes stays EPMoE's, in float32. SGL_PROBE_SHARED=f32 runs the shared expert in
float32 at HIGHEST and adds it in float32. SGL_PROBE_MOE_OUT=f32 keeps the
block's output float32: EPMoE's float32 sum isn't rounded, fc2_latent_proj runs
in float32 at HIGHEST, and the next block's residual add and the capture read
float32 before the stream rounds back. SGL_PROBE_MATMUL=highest sets
jax.default_matmul_precision("highest") over the MoE block and clears it around
the top-k and gmm calls. JAX_DEFAULT_MATMUL_PRECISION=highest over the whole
process reached the Pallas gmm on the slice, and Mosaic refused it ("Bad lhs
type"). A value outside these raises, and the model logs the switches that are
on.

HybridLinearKVPool forwards set_kv_buffer_legacy, the write NativeAttention
takes off TPU, so a CPU engine serves a Nemotron 3 stack that holds an
attention block. The TPU's flash backend never calls it. The Kimi K3 model
patch carries the same forwarding for its own tree.
